11262	The Ming dynasty was the ruling dynasty of China—then known as the Empire of the Great Ming—for 276 years  following the collapse of the Mongol-led Yuan dynasty. The Ming, described by some as "one of the greatest eras of orderly government and social stability in human history," was the last imperial dynasty in China ruled by ethnic Han Chinese. Although the primary capital of Beijing fell in 1644 to a rebellion led by Li Zicheng , regimes loyal to the Ming throne – collectively called the Southern Ming – survived until 1683.
