13411	Otsego County is a county in the U.S. state of New York. As of the 2010 census, the population was 62,259. The county seat is Cooperstown. The name Otsego is from a Mohawk or Oneida word meaning "place of the rock." Otsego County comprises the Oneonta, NY Micropolitan Statistical Area.
